  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Tuesday)\nIssued at 102 PM MDT Tue Oct 6 2026\n\nLatest satellite imagery shows clear skies over the area.\nConditions like this will continue for the next several days.\n\nTemperatures will remain warmer than normal for early October\nthrough the next couple of days. But we'll really feel the warmth\non Friday and Saturday with highs likely reaching the 80s to low \n90s again.\n\nThen a pattern change later this weekend will swing temps in the\nother direction. Highs on the Sunday will range from the 50s in NE\nWY and NW SD to the upper 60s to low 70s in south-central SD.\nBeyond that, highs generally in the 50s are expected. Overnight\nlows will take a dip as well, going from the 40s and 50s to the\n30s and 40s early next week.\n\nAs the weather pattern changes, precip chances will increase\nbeginning Saturday night, lasting into next week. And with the\nmuch colder air from the north, snow is a possibility. That being\nsaid, if snow does happen, it would most likely be at night and in\nthe higher elevations of the Black Hills. Maybe a few flakes mixed\nin with the rain in the plains. So for now, expect mainly rain and\nbe pleasantly (or unpleasantly, depending on your opinion of \nwinter) surprised if you see snow.",
